rac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the left-opening parabola shown above." 13194139535647 true] [17592186359129 1113 #uuid "fd639251-1f6a-5740-8dfa-329f5ae4115a" 13194139535647 true] [17592186359129 1145 "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(-8,4).$\n\nThe general equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-8$ and $y=4$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4)^{2} & =4p(-8) \\\\ 16 & =-32p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=-2x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535647 true] [17592186359130 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359131 13194139535647 true] [17592186359130 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359132 13194139535647 true] [17592186359130 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359133 13194139535647 true] [17592186359130 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359134 13194139535647 true] [17592186359130 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359135 13194139535647 true] [17592186359130 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535647 true] [17592186359130 1041 "selection" 13194139535647 true] [17592186359130 1104 #edb/ref 17592186359133 13194139535647 true] [17592186359130 1110 #uuid "9fa7ac80-0e41-5656-a28a-a763fd0dd171" 13194139535647 true] [17592186359131 1034 "\\frac{4}{y}" 13194139535647 true] [17592186359131 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535647 true] [17592186359131 1111 #uuid "1f5a1c87-0513-55ba-86f0-3ede239e862c" 13194139535647 true] [17592186359132 1034 "-\\frac{1}{2y}" 13194139535647 true] [17592186359132 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535647 true] [17592186359132 1111 #uuid "98f3616f-ff9d-5f02-b530-4721c8d8710f" 13194139535647 true] [17592186359133 1034 "-\\frac{1}{y}" 13194139535647 true] [17592186359133 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535647 true] [17592186359133 1111 #uuid "86000a37-cb17-56c9-9c4d-ac70884a8bd8" 13194139535647 true] [17592186359134 1034 "\\frac{1}{4y}" 13194139535647 true] [17592186359134 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535647 true] [17592186359134 1111 #uuid "e4de1cc8-d105-5589-9c7e-39f1fa8f3425" 13194139535647 true] [17592186359135 1034 "-\\frac{2}{y}" 13194139535647 true] [17592186359135 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535647 true] [17592186359135 1111 #uuid "c818e460-5a42-58d4-8eb8-baf86e9968cd" 13194139535647 true] [17592186359136 1017 #edb/ref 17592186359137 13194139535647 true] [17592186359136 1089 "q-127523" 13194139535647 true] [17592186359136 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535647 true] [17592186359136 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/assets/ebef81911a434828ab94e643007d06b677538cdf0995198c7a065e35a8f81996.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." 13194139535647 true] [17592186359136 1113 #uuid "d416524e-532d-55cb-a87a-c47d846d65e0" 13194139535647 true] [17592186359136 1145 "Since our ellipse is centered at $(-1,-1)$ and has semiaxes $2$ and $1,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-(-1))^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-1))^{2}}{{1}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+(y+1)^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+(y+1)^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((y+1)^{2}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2(x+1)}{4}+2(y+1)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2(y+1)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x+1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x+1}{4(y+1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535647 true] [17592186359137 